From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000109 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:05:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] agent: preserve WSC recovery past device-init command

A strict persistent reconstruction reached an Agent with an associated
backhaul and all three local radio configurations, while the Controller had
only three of its ten BSS records.  The Agent had received all three initial
M2 frames, but OneWifi did not return the provider callback for the first WSC
subdoc.  The subdoc watchdog and the generic device-init command both expired
at 30 seconds.  The generic timeout won the race, cancelled the shared
command, and reset the two incomplete radio state machines to unconfigured.
The protocol retry deliberately made independent of the command lifetime in
the preceding patch therefore had no WSC state left to service.

Treat an incomplete per-radio WSC exchange as protocol-owned when the shared
device-init command expires.  Cancel the stale orchestration command, but
preserve wsc_m2_pending and owconfig_pending so their bounded recovery can
finish without an operator restart.  Other command timeout behavior is
unchanged.

Also make the OneWifi completion watchdog shorter than the command TTL.  Five
seconds is long compared with normal local subdoc application, but leaves
enough time for the existing fresh-crypto M1 retry budget when an RBUS
provider callback is missed.  The retry remains idempotent and bounded.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/agent/em_agent.cpp      |  2 +-
 src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/agent/em_agent.cpp b/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
index 58de17e..6b71f04 100644
--- a/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/agent/em_agent.cpp
@@ -1548,7 +1548,7 @@ void em_agent_t::handle_2s_tick()
 
 void em_agent_t::handle_1s_tick()
 {
-    if (!m_onewifi_wsc_subdoc_active || ++m_onewifi_wsc_wait_ticks < 30) {
+    if (!m_onewifi_wsc_subdoc_active || ++m_onewifi_wsc_wait_ticks < 5) {
         return;
     }
 
diff --git a/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp b/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
@@ -55,9 +55,20 @@ void em_orch_agent_t::orch_transient(em_cmd_t *pcmd, em_t *em)
 
     if (stats->time > EM_MAX_CMD_GEN_TTL) {
         em_printfout("Canceling cmd: %s because time limit exceeded\n", pcmd->get_cmd_name());
+        em_state_t state = em->get_state();
+        em_cmd_type_t cmd_type = pcmd->get_type();
-        cancel_command(pcmd->get_type());
+        cancel_command(cmd_type);
-    	if (em->get_state() < em_state_agent_topo_synchronized) {
+        if (cmd_type == em_cmd_type_dev_init &&
+                (state == em_state_agent_wsc_m2_pending ||
+                 state == em_state_agent_owconfig_pending)) {
+            // WSC is a per-radio protocol transaction and its bounded retry
+            // remains live after the shared device-init command is gone.
+            // Do not erase that ownership state on the generic command TTL.
+            em_printfout("Preserving %s after device-init timeout for radio %s",
+                em_t::state_2_str(state),
+                util::mac_to_string(em->get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str());
+        } else if (state < em_state_agent_topo_synchronized) {
 	    	em->set_state(em_state_agent_unconfigured);
 		} else {
 	    	em->set_state(em_state_agent_topo_synchronized);
 		}
